[38;5;231m⏺[39m Grounding found a real gap in the spec: [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m has no [38;5;153m"type"[39m field, so Node treats [38;5;153m.js[39m as CommonJS. I verified
  empirically on this machine (Node v26.8.2) that [38;5;153mnode --test[39m still runs an ESM [38;5;153mvalidation.js[39m via module-syntax
  detection — it passes, but prints a [38;5;153mMODULE_TYPELESS_PACKAGE_JSON[39m warning. That matters because the obvious "fix"
  (adding [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m) would break [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m, which the spec puts out of scope. The plan pins
  this down so an implementer doesn't wander into it.

